452		 * setModuleServiceLifecycle: So this requires some explanation...
453		 *
454		 * OSGi will start a component once all of it's dependencies are satisfied. However, there are
455		 * times where you want to hold off until the portal is completely ready to go.
456		 *
457		 * This reference declaration is waiting for the ModuleServiceLifecycle's PORTAL_INITIALIZED
458		 * component which will not be available until, surprise surprise, the portal has finished
459		 * initializing.
460		 *
461		 * With this reference, this component activation waits until portal initialization has
462		 * completed.
